 "result_text": "`ariadne` now exports `repair_default_enum_values(schema)` alongside `validate_schema_enum_values`. The test run finished with 616 passed and 8 failed. All 8 failures are websocket tests in `tests/asgi`, and I didn't check whether they also fail without my change.\n\n- **New function:** `repair_default_enum_values` in `ariadne/enums.py` walks every field argument and input field in the schema. It replaces enum default values, including ones nested in input objects and lists, with the Python values bound to the enum members. It takes only the schema; the old version in `executable_schema.py` also took the list of bindables.\n- **`make_executable_schema`:** it now uses the new function and no longer calls `set_default_enum_values_on_schema`.\n- **Exports:** `ariadne/__init__.py` exports `repair_default_enum_values` and no longer exports `set_default_enum_values_on_schema`. That is a breaking change for anyone importing it from `ariadne`. I left the function itself in `enums.py` rather than deleting it.\n\nI didn't add a `CHANGELOG.md` entry.",
